        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dfa30fcc-045c-5e02-b92b-ca972820771a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ronnie Van Zant, Mick Jones, Don Letts, Allen Collins\n- Bands: Lynyrd Skynyrd, The Clash, Big Audio Dynamite\n- Songs and Albums: \"That Smell\", \"Street Survivors\"\n\nFacts:\n- Ronnie Van Zant was born on January 15, 1948, and he became an American lead vocalist, primary lyricist, and founding member of Lynyrd Skynyrd.\n- Mick Jones was born on June 26, 1955, and he became a British musician, singer, songwriter, lead guitarist, co-lead vocalist, cofounder, and songwriter for The Clash.\n- Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins wrote the song \"That Smell,\" which was released in 1977 on the album \"Street Survivors.\"\n- Ronnie Van Zant died on October 20, 1977.\n- Mick Jones was dismissed from The Clash in 1983.\n- In 1984, Don Letts co-founded Big Audio Dynamite with Mick Jones and served as the band's sampler and videographer.\n- Don Letts left Big Audio Dynamite in 1990.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
